---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { url } from '../../lib/url'
---

<Base title="Install" description="Add a Datadog RUM plugin with one script tag, and check the events arrive." docs>
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    One script tag next to your existing RUM snippet. Plugins never call <code>init</code>, so your
    application ID, sampling and privacy settings stay in charge.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Paste the tags</h2>
  <p>Both go before <code>&lt;/head&gt;</code>. Consent plugins go first in <code>plugins</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>{`<script src="https://www.datadoghq-browser-agent.com/us1/v6/datadog-rum.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@kyletaylored/datadog-rum-plugin-onetrust@0.1.0/dist/plugin.js"
        integrity="sha384-REPLACE_FROM_RELEASE" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@kyletaylored/datadog-rum-plugin-woocommerce@0.1.0/dist/plugin.js"
        integrity="sha384-REPLACE_FROM_RELEASE" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script>
  window.DD_RUM.init({
    applicationId: 'YOUR_APPLICATION_ID',
    clientToken: 'YOUR_CLIENT_TOKEN',
    site: 'datadoghq.com',
    service: 'storefront',
    sessionSampleRate: 100,
    plugins: [
      window.DD_RUM_PLUGINS['onetrust']({ category: 'C0002' }),
      window.DD_RUM_PLUGINS['woocommerce'](),
    ],
  })
</script>`}</code></pre>
  <p class="small muted">
    Swap <code>us1</code> for your Datadog site. Versions are pinned and each tag needs the
    <code>integrity</code> hash from that release; there is no <code>latest</code> URL.
  </p>

  <h3>Where to paste it</h3>
  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Shopify</th><td>Settings → Customer events → Add custom pixel. Add the official <code>shopifyPlugin</code> alongside ours; see the <a href={url('/plugins/shopify/')}>Shopify page</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">WordPress / WooCommerce</th><td>Theme header, or a header-scripts plugin. Order data needs a thank-you page payload — see the <a href={url('/plugins/woocommerce/')}>WooCommerce page</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Google Tag Manager</th><td>A Custom HTML tag firing on All Pages, Initialization.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Squarespace / Wix / Webflow</th><td>The site's custom-code or header-injection field.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">A build you control</th><td>Use npm instead — see any plugin page.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Check it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Add <code>{`{ debug: true }`}</code> and reload. Every mapped event prints to the console.
      Nothing printing means the plugin isn't seeing the platform's events — check the page type.
    </li>
    <li>
      Query the RUM Explorer for the cheapest event to produce:
      <pre><code>@type:action @action.name:commerce.add_to_cart</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      Place a test order. Confirm one <code>commerce.purchase</code> with <code>value</code> as a
      number, then reload the thank-you page — a second one must <strong>not</strong> appear.
    </li>
    <li>Import the <a href={url('/docs/datadog-assets/')}>dashboards and monitors</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>3. Reconcile before you trust it</h2>
  <p>
    Compare order count against the platform's admin report over a week. The bar is within 5%.
    Further out is usually one of: declined consent (those visitors send nothing, by design), a
    thank-you page that is never reached, or <code>sessionSampleRate</code> below 100.
  </p>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <p class="small muted">The same on every plugin. Defaults are on each plugin's page.</p>
  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Use it when</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>events</code></td><td class="muted">all</td><td>You only want part of the funnel</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>identifyUsers</code></td><td class="muted"><code>true</code></td><td>Off sends no user ID at all</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>includeEmail</code> / <code>includeName</code></td><td class="muted"><code>false</code></td><td>You have a lawful basis for the session to carry them</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>includeItems</code></td><td class="muted"><code>false</code></td><td>You want line items, up to 20 per action</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>actionPrefix</code></td><td class="muted"><code>commerce.</code></td><td>You have your own naming convention</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>consent</code></td><td class="muted"><code>auto</code></td><td><code>ignore</code> when the page already owns <code>trackingConsent</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>beforeTrack</code></td><td class="muted">none</td><td>You need to edit or drop an event</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>debug</code></td><td class="muted"><code>false</code></td><td>Working out why an event isn't arriving</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p><a class="primary" href={url('/sandbox/')}>Try it before installing →</a></p>

  <div class="next-cards">
    <a class="card" href={url('/sandbox/')}>
      <h3>Sandbox</h3>
      <p>Watch what a plugin sends before you install it.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href={url('/docs/datadog-assets/')}>
      <h3>Dashboards</h3>
      <p>Import the metrics, dashboard and monitors.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href={url('/docs/privacy/')}>
      <h3>Privacy rules</h3>
      <p>Exactly what is and is not sent.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>
